**Root cause: definitively (A)** — the penalized implementation. L2 CV selected C=0.0336, shrinking all 13 scaled coefficients to ≤|0.25|. This produces near-flat propensity scores and breaks the score-equation balance guarantee of overlap weights. Switching to unpenalized MLE restores exact first-moment balance for all model covariates (max |wt SMD| = 0.003).

**However, (C) is also present**: the STRIDE→AB entropy balancing completely collapsed (STRIDE ESS = 1.0). Some STRIDE patients are clinically dissimilar to any AB patient and cannot be credibly balanced to the AB distribution. Overlap weights are the correct estimand precisely because they focus inference on the region of common support — this is confirmed as appropriate.

